{
  "_comment": "What the preprint scan looks for. Everything else (statements, backgrounds, references, dates) is read from data/problems.js and data/site.js. Phrases are matched case-insensitively on title + abstract (and on the full text when it is fetched); hyphens and spaces are interchangeable. A paper is a candidate for a problem when it hits at least one 'topic' phrase AND at least one 'angle' phrase, or when its text similarity to the problem entry reaches 'similarityThreshold'. 'topic' is the problem's subject matter, which other people legitimately work on; 'angle' is what OpenContext's question adds to it. Overlap on the topic alone is ordinary science and is never reported.",

  "arxivCategories": ["quant-ph"],
  "hexagonCategories": ["quant-ph"],
  "lookbackDays": 5,
  "similarityThreshold": 0.22,
  "maxFullText": 25,

